# Uncoil plugin for Claude Code and Cursor

The Uncoil plugin gives Claude Code and Cursor the know-how to set up and debug Uncoil in your project. Ask in plain words and the agent picks the matching skill. It also registers the read-only [Uncoil docs server](/docs/mcp-server), so the agent can read the current documentation instead of relying on memory.

## Install in Claude Code

Add the marketplace and install the plugin:

```text
/plugin marketplace add Uncoil-dev/skill
/plugin install uncoil@uncoil
```

## Install in Cursor

Open **Customize** in the Cursor sidebar, find the Uncoil plugin and select **Install**. On a Teams or Enterprise plan, an admin can instead import `Uncoil-dev/skill` as a team marketplace under **Dashboard, Plugins & MCPs, Import from Repo**.

To try it locally, clone the repository, bundle the plugin into Cursor's local plugin folder and reload the window:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Uncoil-dev/skill
node skill/scripts/bundle.mjs ~/.cursor/plugins/local/uncoil
```

Then run **Developer: Reload Window** and check that the skills and the `uncoil-docs` server show up in **Customize**.

## Other agents

To install only the skills, or to use them in another agent that reads the Agent Skills format:

```bash
npx skills add Uncoil-dev/skill
```

## Skills

| Skill | Use it to |
| --- | --- |
| `uncoil` | Look up docs and apply the SDK rules every Uncoil task needs. |
| `instrument-with-uncoil` | Install the SDK, sign in from the terminal, add tracing and send a first trace. |
| `debug-uncoil-traces` | Find why runs are missing, steps are flat, cost is zero or calls appear twice. |
| `migrate-to-uncoil` | Move tracing from another tool, or point an OpenTelemetry exporter at Uncoil. |

## Examples

- "Add Uncoil tracing to this project."
- "My traces do not show up. Check why."
- "Record thumbs up and down feedback on each run."
- "Move this app from LangSmith to Uncoil."

## Keys and data

The skills never ask you to paste an API key into chat. Signing in runs `npx @uncoil.dev/sdk login`, which saves `UNCOIL_API_KEY` and `UNCOIL_PROJECT_ID` to `.env.local` in the folder. Keep that file out of git. The plugin does not read your traces: project keys send data in, and traces are read in the dashboard.

## Common questions

**Does the plugin need an Uncoil account?**
Only to see traces. Signing in during setup creates the free account if you do not have one.

**Does it work outside Claude Code and Cursor?**
The skills follow the Agent Skills format, so other agents that support it can use them. The plugin install steps are specific to Claude Code and Cursor.

**Where do I report a problem with a skill?**
Open an issue at [Uncoil-dev/skill](https://github.com/Uncoil-dev/skill/issues).
